335
00:25:12.246 --> 00:25:17.878
Design Document (excerpt), Architecture Documentation Standard v1.0.

336
00:25:18.158 --> 00:25:19.054
Status:

337
00:25:19.334 --> 00:25:20.614
Accepted, Authors:

338
00:25:20.894 --> 00:25:22.579
Architecture guild, Reviewers:

339
00:25:22.859 --> 00:25:24.950
Tech leads, SRE, Product.

340
00:25:25.230 --> 00:25:38.393
Context, The slot-booking incident (§1.1) traced to a review that never discussed the key durability decision; diagrams in docs, slides and wikis disagreed with each other and with production.

341
00:25:38.673 --> 00:25:59.430
Decision, One design-doc template (§2.3) for all non-trivial work; C4 model in the repo as the single source of architecture diagrams; automated checks (doc lint, estimation consistency, model validation, drift) in CI; asynchronous-first reviews with named reviewers and recorded outcomes.

342
00:26:00.780 --> 00:26:31.899
Related ADRs, ADR-180 Design-doc template + required sections; ADR-181 docs-as-code under docs or design; ADR-182 C4 model as code, views generated in CI; ADR-183 Doc lint + estimation check as PR checks; ADR-184 Drift detection versus code and trace data, weekly report; ADR-185 Async review,

343
00:26:32.179 --> 00:26:42.653
named asks, recorded outcomes; ADR-186 Design docs are point-in-time, living truth is model + ADRs + generated docs.

344
00:26:42.933 --> 00:26:43.893
Requirements.

345
00:26:44.173 --> 00:26:46.819
R1, Decisions reviewed before they're made.

346
00:26:47.099 --> 00:26:52.389
Every expensive-to-reverse decision appears in a Key decisions section with alternatives.

347
00:26:53.739 --> 00:26:55.787
R2, Measurable requirements.

348
00:26:56.067 --> 00:26:58.307
No NFR without a number (L1).

349
00:26:58.587 --> 00:27:00.422
R3, Consistent numbers.

350
00:27:00.702 --> 00:27:04.435
Derived figures reproducible from stated assumptions (L3).

351
00:27:04.715 --> 00:27:06.827
R4, One source of diagrams.

352
00:27:07.107 --> 00:27:12.782
Context and container views generated from the C4 model; model validated (L2).

353
00:27:13.062 --> 00:27:14.683
R5, True over time.

354
00:27:14.963 --> 00:27:21.982
Documented dependencies diffed against actual dependencies; drift reported weekly and on PRs (L4).

355
00:27:22.262 --> 00:27:24.267
R6, Review has an outcome.

356
00:27:24.547 --> 00:27:26.958
Every review ends with a recorded status.

357
00:27:28.308 --> 00:27:29.716
Decisions in detail.

358
00:27:29.996 --> 00:27:36.652
Template (ADR-180). §2.3; sections may be dropped with a one-line reason.

359
00:27:36.932 --> 00:27:44.591
Docs-as-code (ADR-181). docs or design/.md in the owning repo, reviewed by PR.

360
00:27:44.871 --> 00:27:47.687
Model as code (ADR-182).

361
00:27:47.967 --> 00:27:53.065
Structurizr DSL workspace per domain; CI renders views into the docs site.

362
00:27:53.345 --> 00:27:55.031
(L2 shows the mechanism.).

363
00:27:55.311 --> 00:27:58.041
PR checks (ADR-183).

364
00:27:58.321 --> 00:28:04.508
Lint (L1) and estimation consistency (L3) are warnings on draft, blocking on In review.

365
00:28:05.858 --> 00:28:08.098
Drift (ADR-184).

366
00:28:08.378 --> 00:28:16.570
Dependencies recovered from code and from trace data; undocumented critical-path dependencies raise a ticket to the owning team.

367
00:28:16.850 --> 00:28:17.746
(L4.).

368
00:28:18.026 --> 00:28:20.437
Reviews (ADR-185).

369
00:28:20.717 --> 00:28:27.415
5-day async window, named reviewers with specific asks, meeting only for unresolved disagreements.

370
00:28:27.695 --> 00:28:30.789
Point-in-time docs (ADR-186).

371
00:28:31.069 --> 00:28:37.938
Approved docs are marked Implemented and not maintained; the model, ADRs and generated references are.

372
00:28:38.218 --> 00:28:39.242
