398
00:30:29.613 --> 00:30:41.389
DocLintL1.java, run with: java DocLintL1.java docs or baddesign.md docs or gooddesign.md (JDK 21, no dependencies).

399
00:30:41.669 --> 00:30:43.056
A DESIGN-DOC LINTER.

400
00:30:43.336 --> 00:30:57.075
Most weak design docs fail in the same, mechanically detectable ways: required sections are. missing, non-functional requirements are adjectives instead of numbers (fast, highly available), only one option.

401
00:30:59.925 --> 00:31:00.842
On screen:

402
00:31:01.122 --> 00:31:13.495
Design-doc linter: required sections, measurable NFRs, ≥2 alternatives, real rollout. plan, decision record. docs or baddesign.md (14 lines):

403
00:31:13.775 --> 00:31:15.503
R1 missing section Goals.

404
00:31:15.783 --> 00:31:17.810
R1 missing section Non-goals.

405
00:31:18.090 --> 00:31:21.098
R1 missing section Requirements (NFRs).

406
00:31:21.378 --> 00:31:24.002
R1 missing section Trade-offs or risks.

407
00:31:24.282 --> 00:31:26.650
R1 missing section Observability.

408
00:31:26.930 --> 00:31:28.957
R1 missing section Security.

409
00:31:29.237 --> 00:31:31.647
R1 missing section Open questions.

410
00:31:31.927 --> 00:31:34.509
R2 unmeasurable NFR line 4:

411
00:31:34.789 --> 00:31:37.135
'slow' with no number, then state a target.

412
00:31:37.415 --> 00:31:40.061
R2 unmeasurable NFR line 7:

413
00:31:40.341 --> 00:31:42.623
'fast' with no number, then state a target.

414
00:31:42.903 --> 00:31:44.418
The rest is in the chapter.

415
00:31:47.268 --> 00:31:48.121
Reading it:

416
00:31:48.401 --> 00:31:50.577
The weak doc produced 18 findings:

417
00:31:50.857 --> 00:32:09.631
7 missing sections, 9 adjectives masquerading as requirements (fast, scalable, highly available, secure, real-time, latency will be low), 0 listed alternatives (the only alternative is a passing sentence), a two-word rollout, and no ADR or revisit trigger.

418
00:32:09.911 --> 00:32:14.881
It reads fine, which is exactly why it gets approved without the conversation it needs.

419
00:32:16.231 --> 00:32:18.023
The template-based doc passes.

420
00:32:18.303 --> 00:32:25.471
That doesn't make its design right, it makes it reviewable: every requirement has a number a reviewer can check the design against.

421
00:32:25.751 --> 00:32:35.010
In production, run this as a PR check on docs or design//.md, warning on drafts, blocking when status moves to In review.

422
00:32:35.290 --> 00:32:41.647
Prose linters such as Vale can add style rules (weasel words, passive voice) with the same mechanism.

423
00:32:42.997 --> 00:32:46.261
L2, C4 diagrams generated from one model.

424
00:32:46.541 --> 00:32:47.480
Requirement:

425
00:32:47.760 --> 00:32:52.240
Our context diagram, container diagram, slides and wiki disagree.

426
00:32:52.520 --> 00:32:54.632
Make them impossible to disagree.

427
00:32:54.912 --> 00:33:04.085
The architecture is defined once as a model, people, systems, containers (with owner and technology), relationships (with verb and protocol).

428
00:33:04.365 --> 00:33:08.483
